# Regression fixture for an uncaught std::out_of_range crash found by
# fuzzing (fuzz/fuzz_pipeline.cpp): Parser::intgr() called std::stoi() on
# the literal's text with no try/catch, so a literal too large to fit an
# int (like the one below) threw straight out of main() and aborted the
# whole process instead of being reported as an ordinary parse error.
func mast : int {
  int a = 44444444444444421
  return 0
}
